## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate per-tenant limit adjustments and verification?
- How would you validate rollback in a production window without impacting running builds?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design tenant isolation, per-tenant caching, and robust observability in a shared-kernel environment under bursty load.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant cgroup v2 controls: io.max, memory.max, pids.max
- Per-tenant namespaces and isolated build caches
- BPF/eBPF tracing for vfs, dentry, inode, and I/O paths
- Observability: Prometheus/Grafana, metrics for latency, stalls, cache hits
- Test/rollback: canary tenants, staged rollout, revert quotas

